# PHASE 5, M1 ARM at the 4-iteration budget. Pair file: dd_gate_separation_pi_4iter.tsv, whose
# metadata carries the full analysis of BOTH arms -- read that one for the result.
#
# HOST: CANONICAL111 -- Apple M1 Max, 10 physical cores, aarch64, macOS, g++-16. A working laptop,
#       so the serial/parallel RATIOS are the figure of merit, not the absolute seconds.
# PROTOCOL: identical to the pi arm -- SDPA_BMAT_MODE=sparse, assembly forced serial and parallel,
#       SDPA_BMAT_ASM_PROFILE=1 for the `asm SDP` sub-phase, 3 repeats, medians, shipped param.sdpa
#       with maxIteration -> 4. verdict: win = serial/parallel > 1.5.
# BUILD: dev at the two-bitset commit.
#
# This file exists because an earlier M1 sweep used the shipped param.sdpa UNCHANGED
# (maxIteration=200) while the pi sweep used 4, making the two incomparable in absolute time. This
# is the redo at the matching budget; use it and the pi file together for anything cross-machine.
